Figure 5 illustrates that Nano-11 nanoparticles significantly enhance the uptake of adsorbed antigens by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). Flow cytometry dot plots (A) show a marked increase in both Nano-11 and ovalbumin (OVA) positive cells when OVA is adsorbed to Nano-11, compared to soluble OVA or Nano-11 alone. The histogram (B) further quantifies this, demonstrating a substantial shift in fluorescence intensity for OVA when complexed with Nano-11, indicating a much higher antigen load per cell. This suggests Nano-11 effectively delivers negatively charged antigens to DCs.